TTL (Time To Live) Indexes in MongoDB are special indexes that automaticallyremove documents from a collection
 after a certain period. They are commonly used for data that needs to expire after a specific time, such as session information, logs, or temporary data. To create a TTL index, you can specify the expiration time in seconds

Example: Remove documents 1 hour after createdAt:
db.sessions.createIndex({ "createdAt": 1 }, { expireAfterSeconds: 3600 })